We are building the operating system for go-to-market
This means using AI to help Freshworks understand and act on buyer signals across the full revenue engine. That includes web behavior, for fills, trial activity, intent data, enrichment, account research, meeting transcripts, campaign engagement, and sales activity.&#xa0;
This is an engineering role inside a revenue organization. You will build agents, automations, alerts, data pipelines, and internal tools that help teams move faster and work with better context.&#xa0;
You will build production systems that help marketing and sales prioritize accounts, personalize outreach, route work, surface insights, and reduce manual effort across the buyer journey.&#xa0;
You will have executive support, real production problems, and a clear mandate to define what an AI-native revenue engine looks like across web, marketing, sales, and operations.&#xa0;
What You'll Do
• Build AI-powered GTM workflows.&#xa0; Design and deploy workflows across lead management, account research, routing, scoring, prioritization, personalization, seller briefings, and follow-up support&#xa0;
• Turn buyer signals into action.&#xa0; Build systems that help Freshworks detect, enrich, prioritize, and act on high-value buyer activity across the funnel.&#xa0;
• Create the tool layer for GTM agents.&#xa0; Integrate tools like Salesforce, Clay, Marketo, Relevance, Claude Code, sales engagement platforms, web analytics, enrichment providers, and internal data sources.&#xa0;
• Engineer context pipelines. &#xa0;Bring together data from web activity, intent providers, product usage, firmographics, technographics, meetings, email engagement, and CRM history.&#xa0;
• Build intelligent alerts and recommendations.&#xa0; Create systems that notify teams when important buyer activity happens. This could include target account engagement, key persona activity, competitor mentions, buying committee movement, or stalled follow-up.&#xa0;
• Move prototypes into production.&#xa0; Take working ideas and harden them with authentication, logging, metrics, retries, error handling, alerting, documentation, and cost controls.&#xa0;
• Partner across the revenue engine.&#xa0; Work with Web, Marketing&#xa0;Ops, Sales Ops, Demand Gen, RevOps, SDR and BDR teams, and Engineering to turn business needs into scalable systems.&#xa0;
What We're Looking For&#xa0;
• Engineering experience working with complex systems, varied datasets, and data-driven productivity tools&#xa0;
• Experience as a software engineer, automation engineer, GTM engineer, AI engineer, ML engineer, or technical revenue systems builder
• Hands-on experience building AI or LLM-powered applications, automations, or workflows
• Strong technical skills with APIs, webhooks, OAuth, queues, retries, and system integrations
• Experience integrating CRM systems, marketing automation tools, enrichment tools, sales engagement platforms, lead sources, GitHub, and internal data sources
• Experience with tools or patterns like Claude, OpenAI, Relevance, Clay, MCP, function calling, structured outputs, LangGraph, or custom orchestration
• Experience building automations for lead management, prospecting, routing, qualification, prioritization, or revenue operations
• Strong understanding of inbound and outbound motions
• Ability to translate revenue team needs into technical solutions
• Experience with evals, monitoring, observability, or quality controls for AI systems
• Strong program ownership in ambiguous environments&#xa0;
• Clear communication with technical and non-technical partners
Please note this is a hybrid role with onsite expectations of 3x/week (Tues - Thurs) from our San Mateo, CA headquarters.&#xa0;
The annual base salary range for this position is&#xa0; $202,000 - $250,000.&#xa0; This role is also eligible for a target bonus.&#xa0;
