We are looking to meet talented candidates with at least two years of client-facing experience in data warehousing, data modeling, and analytics engineering, using modern cloud data platforms, in particular Databricks, to build trusted, well-structured data foundations. These foundations power the most impactful customer product offers, marketing campaign strategies, servicing optimization, and/or manufacturing and production improvements.&#xa0;&#xa0;
Key Responsibilities:&#xa0;&#xa0;
Data Modeling and Warehouse Design:&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Design, build, and maintain conceptual, logical, and physical data models for enterprise data warehouses and lakehouses.&#xa0;
• Apply dimensional modeling (star and snowflake schemas, facts and dimensions, slowly changing dimensions) and Data Vault techniques as appropriate to business needs.&#xa0;
• Implement medallion (bronze/silver/gold) architectures on Databricks, using Delta Lake and Unity Catalog.&#xa0;
• Translate business requirements into scalable data models and semantic layers that support reporting, analytics, and data science.&#xa0;
• Optimize warehouse performance and cost through partitioning, clustering, indexing strategies, and efficient compute sizing.&#xa0;
Data Pipelines and Integration:
• Extract data from various sources, including internal databases, data warehouses, APIs, ETL tools, and third-party platforms.
• Develop and maintain ELT/ETL pipelines using Databricks (Spark SQL, PySpark, Delta Live Tables, Workflows) and tools such as dbt and Airflow to automate data workflows.&#xa0;
• Clean, transform, and prepare data for downstream use, ensuring data quality and consistency. This includes handling missing values, outliers, and inconsistencies.&#xa0;
• Develop and maintain automated data quality checks and post-ETL validation tests, including reconciliation back to source systems.&#xa0;
• Implement incremental loading, change data capture (CDC), and orchestration to keep data fresh and reliable.&#xa0;
• Use Git-based version control and CI/CD practices to promote pipeline and data model changes across environments.
Analytics and Reporting Enablement:
• Perform exploratory data analysis (“EDA”) and data profiling to validate data, identify anomalies, and inform model design.&#xa0;
• Build and maintain dashboards and reports on top of the warehouse to track key performance indicators (KPIs) and business metrics, using Power BI, Tableau, or Databricks SQL dashboards.&#xa0;
• Define and maintain consistent business metrics and a governed semantic layer so teams report from a single source of truth.&#xa0;
• Support data scientists and analysts with curated, analysis-ready datasets, and develop predictive or forecasting models as needed.&#xa0;
Data Governance, Security and Best Practices
• Adhere to data governance and security policies and procedures, implementing access controls (role-based access, row- and column-level security, data masking) to ensure data security and privacy.&#xa0;
• Maintain data documentation and contribute to data dictionaries, data lineage, and metadata repositories and catalogs.&#xa0;
• Stay up to date with industry best practices and emerging trends in data warehousing, lakehouse architecture, and data modeling.&#xa0;
• Understand and comply with GDPR/CCPA and data privacy, retention, and confidentiality policies.&#xa0;
Communication and Collaboration
• Present findings, data model designs, and recommendations to stakeholders at all levels of the organization, including senior management.&#xa0;
• Translate complex technical concepts into clear and concise language for non-technical audiences.&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams – product managers, engineers, data scientists, marketing managers – to understand business needs and deliver data-driven solutions.&#xa0;
• Mentor and guide more junior analysts and engineers, providing technical expertise and support.&#xa0;
Education: Bachelor's Degree&#xa0;in a quantitative field such as Statistics, Mathematics, Economics, Computer Science, Information Systems, Data Science, or a related area. Master's degree preferred
Experience: 5-8 years of experience in a data warehousing, data engineering, or data analysis role, with a proven track record of designing and delivering data models and warehouse solutions that drive actionable insights, and/ or consulting experience.&#xa0;
Technical Skills:&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Advanced SQL proficiency is essential, including complex queries, window functions, and performance tuning.&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Hands-on experience with Databricks is essential, including Delta Lake, Unity Catalog, Spark SQL/PySpark, Databricks SQL, and Workflows/Delta Live Tables. Databricks certification is a plus.&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Strong data modeling expertise: conceptual, logical, and physical modeling; dimensional modeling (Kimball star and snowflake schemas, slowly changing dimensions), 3NF, and Data Vault; and medallion/lakehouse architecture patterns.&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Experience with data warehousing concepts and technologies, including ELT/ETL design, incremental loading, change data capture (CDC), and performance and cost optimization.&#xa0;&#xa0;
Familiarity with current Data Platforms:
• Data warehouses and lakehouses: Databricks (preferred), Snowflake, Redshift, or BigQuery&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Databases: SQL Server, Oracle, PostgreSQL, DB2, or MySQL&#xa0;&#xa0;
• APIs and Datasets: MS Dynamics, Oracle CRM, or Salesforce&#xa0;&#xa0;
• ETL/ELT and Orchestration Tools: Databricks Workflows, Delta Live Tables, dbt, Airflow, StreamSets, NIFI, or Kafka or similar&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Cloud Platforms: Azure, AWS, GCP, Oracle, or IBM&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Source Control and CI/CD: Git or GitHub/Gitlab compatible platforms, with experience in CI/CD pipelines&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Data Modeling and Catalog Tools: ERwin, ER/Studio, SqlDBM, or similar; experience with data catalog and lineage tools&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Experience with programming languages such as Python (including PySpark) or Scala for data engineering and analysis.&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Experience with BI tools like Tableau, Power BI, or Looker, including building reports on top of a governed semantic layer.&#xa0;&#xa0;
Analytical Skills:&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Ability to translate business requirements into well-structured, scalable data models.&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Solid understanding of data quality, normalization versus denormalization trade-offs, and performance optimization.&#xa0;&#xa0;
Communication Skills:&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&#xa0;&#xa0;
• Ability to present complex information, such as data models and architecture decisions, clearly and persuasively.&#xa0;
• Proven ability to be a great teammate.&#xa0;
