The Global Research, Informatics & Platform Solutions team within the Information Research (IR) Division partners with scientists and research organizations across AbbVie to unlock the value of scientific data. By enabling effective management, integration, and use of high-quality research data and delivering informatics platforms and decision-support capabilities, the team helps transform complex scientific information into actionable insights that accelerate discovery, strengthen scientific decision-making, and improve the efficiency and effectiveness of research and development. The role serves as a key bridge of expertise between laboratory scientists and technology teams and is responsible for defining, stewarding, and expanding our bioassay knowledge graph, translating scientific workflows into data solutions, and building data visualizations/AI-enabled solutions that accelerate drug discovery.&#xa0;
Responsibilities:&#xa0;
• Perform assigned technical and analytic tasks using established methods and tools, select appropriate approaches for routine problems, document methods and results, and escalate novel or ambiguous issues.&#xa0;
• Execute defined data extraction, transformation, and loading tasks using established tools and scripts.&#xa0;
• Perform data cleaning and preprocessing on moderately complex datasets to prepare for analysis and modeling.&#xa0;
• Conduct basic exploratory data analysis, including generating summary statistics and visualizations to identify trends and anomalies.&#xa0;
• Assist in developing and validating simple statistical models and algorithms under guidance.&#xa0;
• Write and run SQL queries (basic queries, table creation, views, and reporting) to extract, join, and prepare data for analysis and reporting.&#xa0;
• Build dashboards, visualizations, and analyses in standard analytics platforms (e.g., Spotfire, Power BI, Tableau) using established templates and guidance.&#xa0;
• Apply statistical and data mining techniques to scientific datasets, including bioassay data, and interprets results under guidance.&#xa0;
• Support data flow and architecture work, including ETL pipelines, and helps troubleshoot workflows.&#xa0;
• Partner with R&D scientists to understand data needs, and support scientific engagement and user training on delivered solutions.&#xa0;
• Document data workflows, analysis procedures, and experimental results clearly and accurately for team review.&#xa0;
• Deliver reliable outputs for assigned work and small projects, ensure acceptance criteria and compliance, documents methods, communicate progress and escalate high‑impact issues to project leads.&#xa0;
&#xa0;
